# alsa-lib -- the userspace half of ALSA, and the bottom of the audio stack.
#
# Nothing above it can be packaged first: pipewire's ALSA device backend, and
# therefore wireplumber and the GNOME Sound panel, all reach the kernel's sound
# devices through libasound. It links nothing but libc, which is why it is the
# first package of this chain.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://www.alsa-project.org/files/pub/lib/alsa-lib-1.2.14.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=be9c88a0b3604367dd74167a2b754a35e142f670292ae47a2fdef27a2ee97a32
SRC_DIR=alsa-lib-1.2.14

# --disable-python is a DETERMINISM flag, not a feature cut, and it is the only
# non-obvious entry here. configure looks for Python headers and enables the
# experimental mixer python modules when it finds them -- so the same recipe
# would produce a library that links libpython in an image where python happens
# to be installed and one that does not where it is absent, with no error either
# way. Duct packages python, so the ambient answer here is "yes"; deciding it in
# the recipe is what stops the artefact depending on the build image.
#
# EVERY COMPONENT STAYS ON. Each has its own --disable- switch, and the two
# that were measured turn out to fail in OPPOSITE directions -- which is the
# reason install.sh asserts what it does rather than trusting this list:
#   pcm        the device API pipewire's alsa backend opens. LOUD: --disable-pcm
#              does not link libasound at all (make dies on libasound.la), so
#              this one cannot reach a package. Measured, not assumed.
#   topology   libatopology, which the ALSA card profiles read. SILENT:
#              --disable-topology builds, installs and packages perfectly, minus
#              one library. Also measured -- it is what install.sh's
#              libatopology check was controlled against.
#   ucm        Use Case Manager. Every laptop with an SOF/DSP codec routes
#              through UCM profiles rather than raw mixer controls, so a build
#              without it has no sound on most current hardware. Not separately
#              measured; kept on for the hardware reason.
#   mixer, rawmidi, hwdep, seq   the rest of the device APIs
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --disable-python"
